        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> What's the motivation for this?\r\n> \r\n> Also this is a feature, not a fix, since `:checkhealth` is explicitly documented to only check under `$VIMRUNTIME`, `'runtimepath'`, and `'packpath'`.\r\n\r\nThe motivation for this is to support health checking explicitly named modules that lua can load but can't health check. I personally had this issue and also found: [isssue 26580](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/26580). \r\n\r\nSorry for the incorrect title.. should I change it to enhancement? It doesn't allow for wildcard discovery only explicitly nmnamed modules so I don't think it's a feature. Should I document it as well? Or is this out of scope? ",
